### Aggregations:
6. Rolling Aggregations and Summaries:
   - Use rolling_mean, cumsum, and lag on features like loc, v, branchCount to track trends within modules across code segments.
7. Z-Score and Min-Max Scaling: Normalize features to make their relationships more interpretable (e.g., defect-prone modules tend to have outlier values).
8. Derived Defect Metrics: Use b (defects per effort) alongside e/loc and branchCount/loc to highlight density-related defect influencers.

These transformations are expected to enhance the model's ability to identify non-linear and interaction-driven patterns linked to defect-proneness.
